  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1138 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFor this weekend models have continued to trend towards our next\nchance at active weather with a trough moving across the\nSouthwestern United States. Currently latest ensemble runs have\nbeen holding decent confidence in precipitation for the Panhandles\nwith present NBM giving widespread chances ranging from 40 to 80\npercent by Saturday afternoon. These chances will look to hold\nthrough Sunday as most models continue to see the system push\nthrough as moisture continues to wrap around the associated low.\nUnfortunately amounts with these showers has been trending on the\nlighter side with most model runs seeing totals of a few tenths to\nhalf an inch at best. Meanwhile, present mid-range models have\nalso not been too enthused with our potential instability for the\nday, which has resulted in low confidence for strong thunderstorms\nbeing present. Regardless this activity does look to push off by\nnext Monday, only for present model runs to see yet another system\npush in for Tuesday. However, there is still a lot of uncertainty\npresent with this system as present ensembles are only giving the\nPanhandles around a 10 to 30 percent chance of seeing\nprecipitation. Otherwise, look for cooler temperatures to hold\nwith afternoon highs in the upper 50s to 60s, while overnight low\ndrop into the low to mid 30s.",
